Records indicating whether the sexual orientation, gender, or gender identity of candidates was considered — directly or indirectly — in the selection process for the embedded
 positions, including any records reflecting guidance provided to selecting officials regarding Article 92-6 of the Republic of Korea's Military Criminal Act; and any records indicating whether disclosure was provided to, or withheld from, selected personnel
 regarding the legal environment applicable to Article 92-6 aboard the ROKS Dosan Ahn Chang-ho.

This item does not overlap with any of the four items in your revised scope. Items 2 and 3 of your revised wording address the legal and human rights implications of
 Article 92-6 as a general policy matter. The missing item is distinct: it asks specifically whether sexual orientation functioned as an eligibility consideration in the actual selection of the two RCN personnel, and whether those personnel received disclosure
 of the legal environment they would be entering. These are duty-of-care questions at the individual personnel level, not institutional policy questions.

I am prepared to consent to the full revised wording as soon as this item is added. All other elements of the April 17 revised scope are acceptable.

Thank you for your continued assistance.

